he corrected evidence-based claim. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison. Name its specific science error, then show the corrected evidence-based claim.","Changing the wording without repairing the evidence does not fix the error. A game with no way to win or lose is unfinished for this lesson’s purpose.","Treat a missing measurement as if it were recorded.","Skip the fair-test idea because the first guess looked neat."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Test a misconception\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the same science idea on a new object, material or context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy of observations. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use the same science idea on a new object, material or context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy of observations.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new evidence.","Skip the fair-test idea because the first guess looked neat.","Ignore the observation and invent a more exciting result."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Transfer to a new investigation\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"e.g. catch fruit; left/right keys; catch 5 to win. Useful feedback uses the original observations and method.","options":["e.g. catch fruit; left/right keys; catch 5 to win.","A game with no way to win or lose is unfinished for this lesson’s purpose.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"List goal, one control and one win condition for a tiny catcher game.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The most useful record names the evidence and the reason it supports the claim, not only a label. Useful feedback uses the original observations and method.","options":["The most useful record names the evidence and the reason it supports the claim, not only a label.","Writing only a final label without evidence does not show scientific thinking.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"List the key observations or steps from the model and say what each one shows.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"e.g. catch fruit; left/right keys; catch 5 to win. Useful feedback uses the original observations and method.","options":["e.g. catch fruit; left/right keys; catch 5 to win.","Changing the wording without repairing the evidence does not fix the error. A game with no way to win or lose is unfinished for this lesson’s purpose.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Describe why the warned-against claim fails, then write a corrected claim with e\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The new example should use the same science idea as the model, but contain different objects or data. Useful feedback uses the original observations and method.","options":["The new example should use the same science idea as the model, but contain different objects or data.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new evidence.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Investigate or describe one fresh example that uses the same skill and write a s\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence, not repetition of the worked model, demonstrates the skill.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced relevant evidence with accurate reasoning and named observations.","question":"Investigate or describe a fresh example that uses the central skill. Show evidence and name the observations that matter.","sample_answer":"Original demonstration: Goal: catch three stars. Controls: arrow keys move. Win: score 3. Test if stars are too fast — adjust speed block.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A correction needs to change the claim or evidence, not just make the notes longer.","marking_guide":"Require an actual misconception plus corrected claim and an evidence-linked reason.","question":"Name one likely science misconception for this topic, correct it and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Common error: A game with no way to win or lose is unfinished for this lesson’s purpose. Correction: e.g. catch fruit; left/right keys; catch 5 to win.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent evidence and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-sci-y3-w29-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA Science and Technology alignment using catalogue outcome codes; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise game.","Read the mission before you start observing or testing.","Keep the property or variable you are studying in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your evidence with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the observation or step that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore observations or fair tests.","Prefer accurate evidence over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your evidence and reason are both present.","Proofread labels, measurements and sequence of steps.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title an